# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# `cargo mero build` writes the contract into the app's res/ alongside abi.json.
# The ABI and state schema ARE committed (CI regenerates and diffs them); the
# wasm is build output, so ignoring it is what keeps a local build from leaving
# the tree dirty and a stray binary from being committed by `git add -A`.
apps/*/logic/res/*.wasm
# A multi-service app keeps its extra service crates in logic/crates/<name>/, and
# `cargo mero bundle` writes each one's wasm into its own res/. The glob above is
# non-recursive, so without this line those land untracked and `git add -A`
# commits a binary. Their abi.json/state-schema.json ARE still committed.
apps/*/logic/crates/*/res/*.wasm

# Node
node_modules/
# Anchored to where builds actually write, so a source directory named `dist`
# cannot be ignored by accident.
apps/*/app/dist/
apps/*/app/dist-types/
*.tsbuildinfo

# merobox drops several hundred MB of node state here.
# Anchored: an unanchored `data/` would also swallow a source directory called
# `data` at any depth, silently.
/data/
apps/*/data/
apps/*/logic/data/
apps/*/logic/workflows/data/

# Signed bundles are build output; the registry is the distribution channel
dist/*.mpk
apps/*/logic/dist/

# Local env
.env
.env.local

# ⚠️ Written by the e2e provisioners (mero-drive's scripts/e2e-up.ts, and the
# equivalent for battleships) and it holds LIVE JWT access AND refresh tokens
# for the local nodes. Only mero-drive's own .gitignore covered it, so for the
# other 15 apps the file sat untracked — one `git add -A` from being committed.
# Ignored repo-wide, and `.env.integration.example` stays committable.
.env.integration
*.local

# Playwright
test-results/
playwright-report/
# ⚠️ Root-level, not per-app. `apps/meropixart/.gitignore` carried
# `app/e2e-artifacts/`, which stops covering the files the moment the directory
# is renamed on another branch — and untracked files survive a branch switch, so
# a `git add -A` there commits Playwright output under a path no rule reaches.
# That happened twice, and the second time it made check-vercel-output.sh report
# a phantom app (`mero-pixart NO vercel.json`) and fail the Frontend job.
e2e-artifacts/
# Node home + logs the browser e2e global-setup creates.
.playwright-data/
blob-report/

# OS
.DS_Store

# tsc -b declaration output
dist-types/

# Python bytecode from scripts/ helpers.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
